    "narrative": "Our core focus for today\u2019s slate centers on **Corbin Carroll** and **Austin Riley**, both of whom anchor our lineup with scores near the 70-point threshold. **Corbin Carroll** remains an essential start against the vulnerable Alec Gamboa; despite a slight platoon penalty for hitting left-on-left, his proximity to the top of the order and the favorable park environment keep his floor high. Meanwhile, **Austin Riley** presents the most intriguing upside of the day. Facing Ober with a 4.81 xERA, **Austin Riley** benefits from a massive 19% boost due to the starter's poor metrics and a wind-out scenario that should elevate his power profile. Even with an order position deep in the lineup, his individual matchup quality outweighs the potential for fewer plate appearances.\n\nElsewhere, the decision to play **Seiya Suzuki** despite facing Luis Castillo is driven by his resilience against tough right-handed arms and his high-volume hitting position. He remains a stronger play than **Gabriel Moreno** or **Zach McKinstry**, both of whom are relegated to the marginal tier (sub-60) due to shaky matchups or defensive-heavy lineup placements. **Mickey Moniak** serves as our primary risk today; while his score of 45.71 technically qualifies as a start, he is a candidate for a late-game swap should we need to protect our remaining game caps. His poor score is heavily influenced by the presence of Blake Snell, whose elite 2.39 xERA and low SB-allowance rate drastically depress the value of any lefty facing him.\n\nWith **Jose Caballero** and **Josh Naylor** out today due to team off-days, our bench remains largely inactive, though we are closely monitoring the status of **James Wood** and **Trevor Story** as they continue their respective stints on the IL. We are currently prioritizing the health of our prospect pool\u2014including **Dalton Rushing**, **Travis Bazzana**, **Edwin Arroyo**, **Cole Young**, and **Henry Bolte**\u2014over risky mid-season waiver additions. For now, we are comfortable rolling with the current configuration, banking on the power upside of **Giancarlo Stanton** and **Vinnie Pasquantino** to support the speed-focused contributions of **Corbin Carroll** and **Brice Turang** in future rotations. Keep an eye on lineup confirmations; should **Gabriel Moreno** drop out of the #3 spot, his efficiency score will likely plummet below our threshold.",
